 -- Keel Linux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:00:06 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel3) trixie; urgency=low

  * Instance menu: add Database mode, the console half of handbook decision
    0013. Standalone, or Cloud splitting into Primary and Replica, each
    leading to a screen that configures THIS node and nothing else: the
    addresses it answers on, the origins a primary allows to replicate from
    it, the endpoint a replica replicates from, and the file holding the
    replication credential. A prefix is offered as the form to prefer and a
    name is called fragile, which is what docs/spec.md of keel says.
  * Every cloud screen states, in a line the operator cannot miss, that this
    replication has no automatic failover: if the primary stops, nothing
    takes over by itself.
  * Promote this replica is its own entry, and asks first, because promoting
    while the old primary still runs leaves two writable servers holding one
    dataset. It says so in the question.
  * Becoming a replica replaces the local database. The screen never decides
    that: it shows keel's own refusal and asks whether to go on, and only a
    Yes adds --destroy-local-database to the run.
  * What the operator typed is staged beside the description and handed to
    keel spec validate before it replaces it, so a value that would not load
    cannot replace one that does.
  * Depend on python3-yaml: the menu writes the description it collected.

 -- Marcos Méndez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:50:00 +0000

confconsole (2.2.3+keel2) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add the Instance menu: view the instance description, apply it, show the
    drift between it and the machine, and export what the machine says as a
    description. The menu is a front end over the keel client (keelcli), so
    the console and the command line answer from the same code.
  * Usage screen: put the mark above it, dropping to the small mark and then
    to none before the addresses lose a line, so a serial console and an
    80x24 terminal both render it.
  * Recommend keel rather than suggest it: the Instance menu calls it, and
    without it the menu says so instead of failing, so it stays a
    recommendation and the package remains installable on its own.

